<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπώμ-οτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abjured, declared
				impossible on oath,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρημάτων ἄελπτον οὐδέν ἐστιν οὐδ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
					74
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βροτοῖσιν οὐδέν ἐστ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					388
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγμ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					217
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲν ἀ. οὐδὲ ἄπρακτον ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					4.102
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>under oath not to do a thing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καίπερ ὢν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					394
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἀν ἀ. τις ᾖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
					566
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
